  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An operator evaluates a runtime model, and the eval policy writer records it in routing/policy.json. Later they delete the model through the API, which succeeds. On the next restart the daemon refuses to start because the policy file names an unknown model.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/adj/c3.ts  (add runtime codex/experiment; policy.json {triage:{default:['codex/experiment']}} loaded via readPolicy into Router; catalog.remove; readPolicy again with code + stored runtime models)",
    "output": "DELETE succeeded\nrestart fails: Error: Invalid routing policy .../policy.json: [ { \"code\": \"custom\", \"message\": \"Error: unknown model ID \\\"codex/experiment\\\"\" ..."
   },
   "evidence": "remove() (lines 79-87) checks only store.routingCells(). Unlike patch() at line 71, it never calls validatePolicy(this.router.getPolicy(), ...). Factory.evalPolicy passes this.models, which includes runtime models, to the eval policy writer, so `eval policy --write` can name a runtime model. At startup, app.ts calls readPolicy(opts.policyPath, this.models, ...), and that throws."
  }
 },
